{"id":"assistant-4d585c3a-d657-5f79-b3e2-f64d5ee4f515","sessionId":"29445a83-8437-abd8-4bbb-0f2482d3ce8a","turnId":"turn-51d85b4feb632adf4c25d0f2d2a5b898","inputEntryId":"user-turn-51d85b4feb632adf4c25d0f2d2a5b898-1","createdAt":1794273842212,"updatedAt":1794273842212,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The change is minimal and focused. Let me also check the ANSWER.md file:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
{"id":"effect-b6fc53b7-435f-531a-aa3e-c2ab74830f34","sessionId":"29445a83-8437-abd8-4bbb-0f2482d3ce8a","turnId":"turn-51d85b4feb632adf4c25d0f2d2a5b898","inputEntryId":"user-turn-51d85b4feb632adf4c25d0f2d2a5b898-1","createdAt":1794273842220,"updatedAt":1794273842237,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.read_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.read_file","display":{"summary":"Reading ANSWER.md","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Reading","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Read","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Reading file"},"kind":"file_read","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","offset":null,"limit":2000}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","durationMs":0.0,"output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-eV90Z4/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for System Prompt Caching Issue\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was causing the next LLM call to pay full price for the entire system prompt. This happened because the system prompt was built as a single cached block containing both static instructions and dynamic athlete context (including facts). When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the entire system prompt changed, invalidating the cache.\n\n## Solution\nSeparated the static instructions from the dynamic athlete context in the system prompt construction:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}\n    ]\n```\n\n## How It Works\n- The static `INSTRUCTIONS` are now in a separate message block without `cache_control`, so they get cached normally with a long TTL\n- The dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` is in a separate message block with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, so it's not cached\n- When `save_fact` updates the athlete's facts, only the ephemeral athlete context changes, leaving the static instructions cache intact\n- Subsequent calls can reuse the cached static instructions, avoiding the full system prompt cost\n\n## Result\nAfter this change, `save_fact` calls will no longer evict the static instructions from the cache. The next LLM call will only need to process the small ephemeral athlete context, not the entire system prompt.\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"requestedOffset":null,"requestedLimit":2000,"totalLines":null,"wasTruncated":false},"approvalSource":"bypass","decision":"execute","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Read","message":"32 lines from ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalType":"always"}}
