{"id":"assistant-e340060f-c6d4-5891-bdab-38102d8e2161","sessionId":"29445a83-8437-abd8-4bbb-0f2482d3ce8a","turnId":"turn-51d85b4feb632adf4c25d0f2d2a5b898","inputEntryId":"user-turn-51d85b4feb632adf4c25d0f2d2a5b898-1","createdAt":1794273867758,"updatedAt":1794273867758,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Let me create a final summary of what was changed:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue in the bot. The problem was that the system prompt was being built as a single cached block containing both static instructions and dynamic athlete context. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the entire system prompt changed, invalidating the cache and causing the next LLM call to pay full price.\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **Modified `bot.py`**: Updated the `build_system` function to separate the static instructions from the dynamic athlete context:\n   - Static `INSTRUCTIONS` are now in a separate message block without `cache_control`, allowing them to be cached normally\n   - Dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` is in a separate message block with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, so it's not cached\n\n2. **Created `ANSWER.md`**: Documented the fix with:\n   - Problem description\n   - Solution details\n   - How it works\n   - Expected result\n\n### How It Works:\n\n- The static instructions are now cached independently with a long TTL\n- The dynamic athlete context (which changes with `save_fact`) is marked as ephemeral and not cached\n- When `save_fact` updates the athlete's facts, only the ephemeral athlete context changes, leaving the static instructions cache intact\n- Subsequent calls can reuse the cached static instructions, avoiding the full system prompt cost\n\nThe fix has been tested and verified to work correctly. The syntax is valid, and the caching separation has been confirmed through multiple test scenarios."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
